  "notes": "USAGE:\n{具現|ぐげん} is a formal, literary word. It is often used with する to form a verb meaning \"to embody\" or \"to realize in concrete form.\" The related form {具現化|ぐげんか} (making concrete, materialization) is also common.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {具現|ぐげん}する (to embody, to realize)\n- {具現化|ぐげんか}する (to materialize, to make concrete)\n- {理想|りそう}の{具現|ぐげん} (embodiment of an ideal)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {体現|たいげん}: embodiment (through one's own body or actions)\n- {実現|じつげん}: realization, achievement (more general and common)\n- {具体化|ぐたいか}: making concrete (less literary)",
